WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.835
-My next guest is an Oscar
and Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.705
who stars in the Fox series
"9-1-1."

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.675
Season 4 premieres this Monday
at 8:00 p.m.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.610
Here is the one and only
Angela Bassett.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.513
Oh, come on, look at you.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.848
-Hey!
-Oh, it's so great to see you.

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:16.983
Ah, you look great.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.519
Thank you for coming on again.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.987
I hope the family's all well.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.389
Are your --
How old are the kids now?

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.690
Are they --

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.727
-They are soon to be 15
in just a couple of weeks.

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:31.264
In about two weeks,
they'll be 15 years old.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.598
-Wow.
-Yeah. They're doing good.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:35.368
-What's it like to quarantine
with two 14-year-olds

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.936
the past few months?

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:40.673
-You know, they spend
an extraordinary amount of time

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:41.541
in their rooms.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.042
They did before quarantine.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:46.780
But now with that in-school
Zooming, even more so.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.515
So I kind of hardly see them

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:52.084
except at, like, dinner,
making breakfast.

00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:55.188
-Yeah. They go, "Yeah,
we're good, Mom. We're good."

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.423
-Yeah, I think they're cool
with that.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:00.960
-You've always done
this cool thing where you start

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.962
every post on social media
asking --

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.697
you say, "Everybody good?"

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:08.501
And this is before the pandemic,
before COVID.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.903
And do you feel like
people are responding

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.173
to that now even more?

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.641
-Yeah. I find that they are.

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:18.177
I mean, they were before,
but even so now.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:19.679
Some folks have gone through,

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.481
you know,
extraordinary, hard times.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.849
So they appreciate just,
you know,

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:27.319
just that asking about
how everything's going.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.622
-Last year was tough
for so many reasons,

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:33.293
but we also lost your good
friend, Chadwick Boseman.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:36.596
But there's a story here
that you actually met

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.897
before "Black Panther."

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:38.898
Would you mind
telling the story?

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.933
-We did. We did.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:45.003
Yeah, a number of years ago
I was -- I was so honored

00:01:45.003 --> 00:01:48.474
to receive an honorary doctorate
from Howard University.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:49.909
And so I'd go there.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:52.378
It was a great time,
a great experience, whatever.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.847
And, you know, life goes on.
You go back to doing your work.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:58.651
And I get this movie,
you know, "Black Panther."

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.319
I'm sitting next to Chadwick.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.921
Every morning we shared

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:05.191
the same makeup trailer,
same hair trailer.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.026
So we spend hours and hours,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.229
you know, prepping the day,
getting ready.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.663
I'm watching him, you know,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.966
call South Africa,
get his dialect right, you know.

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:17.403
And so the night of the
premiere -- glorious premiere.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.039
You know, pinnacle of
just everything.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.108
Cherry on top, whatever,
and I'm looking --

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.910
you know, getting ready
to leave, take the kids.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.177
The only premiere
I've taken them --

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:27.613
one of the few premieres
I've taken them to.

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:28.948
We're getting ready to leave.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:29.982
Let me go say hello,

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:32.151
and I find him
and give him an embrace.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:33.552
It's just been incredible.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.187
And he whispers in my ear.

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:37.623
He said, "When you got
your honorary degree,

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:41.661
I was the student that escorted
you throughout that day."

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.797
And I was just so blown away.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.901
I couldn't believe that
he held that back from me...

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.703
-Wow, for the whole shooting.
-...until this very moment.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.472
While we were shooting.
Yeah, the entire time.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.374
But he shared that.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:58.043
And, you know, so many times
you meet young people.

00:02:58.043 --> 00:02:59.979
And they say, "Oh, I want to
work with you one day."

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.482
And you know that, you know,
you say, "Yeah, I hope so too."

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:06.485
But you know how rare
that can be, you know.

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:08.821
But we actually did.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.589
We actually did work together.

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:12.258
-Do you remember years ago,
by the way,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.394
you gave me a ride
to an awards show.

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:18.230
-It was after the Oscars
one night.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.532
-Yeah. You remember that?

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.034
-Yeah. I think we shared
the same manager or something.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.135
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:24.770
-And we were in
the backseat together.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.739
-I loved it.
I'll never forget it.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.441
I was like, "You are -- I can't
believe I'm with Angela Bassett.

00:03:29.441 --> 00:03:30.776
She's so cool."

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:32.712
-I've never forgotten it too,
because you were so cool.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.313
You were as nice then
as you are now.

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:36.782
So yeah, I always remember
that too.

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:39.485
-We were doing some research
about you,

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:43.056
and I saw that your very first
TV gig, your first job,

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:46.425
was exactly 35 years ago
on a soap opera

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:48.294
called "Search for Tomorrow."

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.464
-Yes, "Search for Tomorrow,"
right out of drama school.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:54.400
And I thought
it was such a big deal.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.901
I think I had
a little, small role.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:59.505
I think I was a nurse
and someone's sister,

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.173
big sister to someone.
-Yeah.

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:04.010
When was the last time
you saw it?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.279
-35 years ago.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.379
Definitely.

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.315
-Well, we actually found
a clip of you

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:13.252
from a 1985 episode of
"Search for Tomorrow."

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.421
Watch this.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.489
-How's it going, Salina?

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:19.124
-Well, well, look what
the wind blew in.

00:04:19.124 --> 00:04:20.192
Hmm?
-You're mad, right?

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:21.694
-Only dogs get mad.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.195
-Okay, so you're angry?

00:04:23.195 --> 00:04:25.197
-Do I look angry?

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:26.265
-What do you think?

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.433
-Well, by the look in your eye,

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.201
I'd say it's not one
of your better days.

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:31.404
-Oh, you read me right.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.804
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.804 --> 00:04:34.940
-My voice is so high.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.041
-Oh.

00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:37.509
-"You read me right."

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:38.911
-And look at you now.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.280
I want to talk about "9-1-1."

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.950
Season 4 premieres on Monday.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.753
This show is all about
first responders.

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:49.555
So can you set up
what's going on this season?

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.592
'Cause it was a crazy episode
the end of last season.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.627
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:57.763
At the end of last season,
you know, Athena was --

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:00.633
I mean,
she was brutally attacked.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.236
And, of course,
she's been healing.

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:06.873
And the physical -- the physical
wounds have healed,

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.807
the face, the arm, whatever.

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:11.677
But what about her
emotionally, mentally?

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:13.545
That's where we're at.

00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:16.648
But also, as we know
in this world, you know,

00:05:16.648 --> 00:05:20.686
trauma and tragedy is
around each and every corner.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:25.057
And as it opens up, there's been
this huge sort of, like,

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:27.192
break at
the Hollywood Reservoir,

00:05:27.192 --> 00:05:31.631
and there's sludge and mudslides
that's taking down --

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:36.435
just taking down neighborhoods
and iconic signs and everything.

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:39.805
And first responders --
there's never a day off.

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.073
So either she's going to run in

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:42.608
and help
or she's going to retreat.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:45.143
-Of course.
-And we see what happens.

00:05:45.143 --> 00:05:47.613
-You do a great job.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:50.750
Here's Angela Bassett in
the season premiere of "9-1-1."

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.117
Take a look.

00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:54.387
-They are not thinking on
their feet out there.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:56.255
It's more like their elbows.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:59.225
-Got an alarming call from
the emergency operations center.

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.727
They think those micro quakes

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.995
might've damaged
more than just the dam.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:06.332
They're worried about a
landslide east of the reservoir.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.033
-East of the reservoir.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.535
Well, that's all residential.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.169
You're going to need more boots
on the ground,

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:12.538
people to knock on doors.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.707
-And someone to supervise
the scene.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:17.276
Look, I know you said
you wanted to ease in,

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:19.345
but I need you back out there.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.153
-Angela Bassett.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:29.088
Season 4 of "9-1-1" premieres

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.723
Monday at 8:00 p.m. on Fox.

00:06:31.723 --> 00:06:33.492
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:34.560
You know I love you.

